    "description": "<p>The world calls them Razz Hackers. They call themselves Neo Monks—adepts who treat spellwork and software as the same living language running beneath neon streets and astral skylines.</p><p>Nobody teaches you how to become a Razz Hacker. You learn it the hard way: by realizing magic and code aren’t opposites or “two paths.” They are the same interface—syntax that convinces reality to compile.</p><p>Once it clicks, you move through the world differently: you slip through an ICE wall as a freezing sigil in the datasphere, or you fire an arcane pulse packaged as perfectly structured JSON.</p><p></p>",
